<rml>
<head>
	<title>Contain: paint</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="../style.rcss"/>
	<link rel="help" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-contain-2/#paint-containment" />
	<meta name="Description" content="Paint containment clips overflowing content, and makes the element the containing block of absolutely positioned descendants." />
	<style>
		body {
			display: block;
			background: #ddd;
			color: #444;
		}
		div.contain {
			contain: paint;
			border: 1dp black;
			width: 200dp;
			height: 80dp;
			margin: 10dp 0;
		}
		div.wide {
			width: 300dp;
			height: 20dp;
			color: #f00;
			text-align: right;
			background-color: #aaa;
		}
		div.absolute {
			position: absolute;
			top: 90dp;
			left: 0;
			width: 80dp;
			height: 80dp;
		}
		div.list {
			overflow: auto;
			width: 200dp;
			height: 120dp;
			border: 1dp black;
		}
		div.row {
			contain: paint;
			height: 30dp;
			margin: 5dp;
			border-radius: 5dp;
		}
		.green { background-color: #7f7; }
		.red { background-color: #f77; }
	</style>
</head>

<body>
<p>There should be no red visible, and the word 'fail' should not appear.</p>
<div class="contain">
	<div class="wide">FAIL</div>
	LONG_WOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOORD&nbsp;FAIL
	<div class="absolute red">Should not be visible</div>
</div>
<div class="list">
	<div class="row green">1</div>
	<div class="row green">2</div>
	<div class="row green">3</div>
	<div class="row green">4</div>
	<div class="row green">5</div>
	<div class="row green">6</div>
	<div class="row green">7</div>
	<div class="row green">8</div>
</div>
</body>
</rml>
